# euiccCiPKIdListForVerification hand-edited to drop the second entry,
# F54172BDF98A95D65CBEB88A38A1C11D800A85C3 -- byte-for-byte the
# SubjectKeyIdentifier of euicc-rsp's testdata/sgp26/ci.der, our test
# Certificate Issuer (src/card.c's test_ci_ski). The list's own length (the
# "A9" TLV, 2C -> 16) and the enclosing EUICCInfo2's length (the "BF22"
# TLV, 81F8 -> 81E2, 22 bytes shorter) are the only two other bytes that
# had to change; nothing else in this recording is touched, including the
# untouched euiccCiPKIdListForSigning ("AA2C", not read by
# rsp_card_read_info at all) a few bytes later, which still lists both
# identifiers.
#
# `euicc card info --replay` against this file must exit 1, not 0: this
# (edited) card answers, and its remaining issuer is not the one our test
# credentials chain to.
